; expect 7
;
; The control that must stay SILENT, and the file that named what had
; to be built before it could.
;
; IT MOVED HERE ON 2026-08-25, out of the diagnostics corpus where it
; was case 351, and the move is the point. A diagnostics fixture whose
; golden is empty is refused by that corpus - "a case that diagnoses
; nothing proves nothing" - and it was right to refuse this one: once
; the analysis learned the difference, this file stopped making a claim
; about a DIAGNOSTIC and started making one about a PROGRAM. It
; compiles, it runs, and it answers 7. `tests/diagnostics/352-tyvar-delegation.ax`
; keeps the silent half where a diagnostics corpus can hold it, beside
; three errors.
;
; `347-result-only-tyvar.ax` is the unsound shape: a body that CASTS a
; machine word out through a result type the caller picks. This file is
; the other one AX3040 used to conflate with it, and it is a CORRECT
; PROGRAM.
;
; `panic` promises `forall a. String -> a`. That signature is inhabited
; only by non-termination - `explain AX3040` says so in those words -
; and `panic` is exactly that inhabitant: every path through it reaches
; `exit`, so it never returns and never produces a value of the type
; the caller named. Nothing is coerced, nothing is dereferenced, and no
; caller can observe a wrong answer, because no caller is resumed.
;
; It is a shape a real program wants. A checked accessor, an assertion,
; an unrecoverable configuration error - each is a function whose type
; is honestly `forall a`, called in a position that expects an `Int` or
; a `String` and simply never gets there.
;
; MEASURED 2026-08-24, both paths, and again 2026-08-25 after the
; promotion:
;
;     (pick 7)        -> exits 7,  `panic` never entered
;     (pick (- 0 1))  -> writes "negative" to fd 2 and exits 70
;
; so the program is right on the path that returns AND on the path that
; does not.
;
; WHAT THIS FILE USED TO SAY, and what happened. It said: "What
; promotion needs first is a way to tell divergence from a cast: a
; spelling for `does not return`, or a walk proving every path exits.
; Until one exists, this file is the control that keeps the shape
; visible - if it ever stops drawing AX3040, something learned the
; difference and `severity.policy` should be re-read."
;
; It stopped drawing AX3040 on 2026-08-25. The walk exists, and this
; file is now the control in the OTHER direction: its golden is empty,
; and any diagnostic appearing here is the analysis losing the
; distinction it was built for.
;
; HOW THE WALK ADMITS THIS ONE, which is worth stating because the
; shape below is the reason the analysis is not simply "the tail must
; not be a cast". `panic`'s tail IS a cast - `(cast a (exit 70))` -
; and it diverges anyway, because the value being coerced is `(exit
; 70)`, which never returns: `IO.exit` ends in `sysExitWith`, and a
; cast whose argument never returns is unreachable and fabricates
; nothing. An analysis that looked only at the head of the tail would
; have refused the program this fixture exists to protect.
;
; `sound` is the control in the third direction and must stay silent
; for a different reason entirely: `a` appears in a PARAMETER, so the
; caller supplies a value of it and the choice is witnessed by the
; argument.
(import IO)

(:: panic (-> String a))

(fn (panic msg)
  {
    (writeStr 2 msg)
    (cast a (exit 70))
  }
)

(:: sound (-> a a))

(fn (sound x) x)

(:: pick (-> Int Int))

(fn (pick n)
  (if (< n 0)
    (panic "negative\n")
    n
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (pick 7))
